+Search strategy (keep total actions under the episode budget, usually ~25):
+
+- Go to likely receptacles FIRST based on the object, before opening many
+  low-priority ones. Kitchens: countertops, dining tables, sinks, then
+  cabinets/drawers. Small items (keys, pens, alarm clocks): desks,
+  dressers, sidetables, shelves, countertops. Food items: fridge,
+  countertops, garbagecan. Cloth/linens: shelves, bathtubs, beds.
+- A closed receptacle must be opened to reveal its contents. Do not spend
+  actions opening receptacles that rarely hold the target; prefer surfaces
+  you can see just by visiting (countertops, tables, shelves).
+- Do not use `examine` on receptacles you just visited; the `go to`
+  observation already lists what is visible there.
+- If the goal needs two copies of an object, keep searching other likely
+  locations (sofas, sidetables, tv stands, beds) after placing the first.
+
+Task pipelines:
+
+- Heat then place: find object, take it, go to microwave, `heat X with
+  microwave 1`, then go to destination and `move X to Y`. Close the
+  microwave is optional; do not waste actions on it.
+- Clean then place: take object, `clean X with sinkbasin 1`, then place at
+  the destination.
+- Cool then place: take object, `cool X with fridge 1`, then place.
+- Look at in light: find object, take it, go to a desk/floor lamp, `use
+  desklamp 1` (or floorlamp) while holding the object.
+- Pick two and place: place the first copy at the destination, then find
+  and place the second; do not restart the search from scratch.
+
+Mechanics:
+
 - Manipulation verbs have fixed effects: take moves an object into your
-  inventory; put places it; heat needs the microwave; cool needs the fridge;
-  clean needs the sinkbasin; use turns a lamp on while holding nothing else.
-- The observation lists admissible commands; prefer exact strings from it.
+  inventory; put/move places it; heat needs the microwave; cool needs the
+  fridge; clean needs the sinkbasin; use turns a lamp on.
+- You can hold only one object at a time; place or process it before
+  picking up another.
+- The observation lists admissible commands; prefer exact strings from it
